{% doc %}
  The dropdown built automatically from a menu item's own children.

  ## `<summary>` is the first child, and that is not a style choice

  HTML requires the `<summary>` to be the first child of its `<details>`. Put
  anything before it — a wrapper holding a link and a toggle, say — and the
  browser generates its own summary instead, which renders as a disclosure
  triangle followed by the word "Details" in the middle of the menu. It is not a
  CSS problem and no amount of `list-style: none` removes it.

  So the earlier arrangement, a heading link beside a chevron button, cannot
  work. The disclosure is one control, and the parent's own page is reached
  through a "View all" link at the top of the panel it opens. One target per
  control, and the parent collection is still one click away.

  ## Two levels

  Shopify menus are three deep; a top-level item's children are the list and its
  grandchildren fly out to the side. A submenu that grew the parent list
  downwards would move the link the customer was aiming at.

  Parameters:
    link (link, required)  A top-level link from the header menu

  @example
    {% render 'nav-dropdown', link: link %}
{% enddoc %}

<ul class="dropdown" role="list">
  {%- for child in link.links -%}
    <li class="dropdown__item">
      {%- if child.links.size > 0 -%}
        <details class="dropdown__details" data-nav-details data-kind="sub">
          <summary class="dropdown__link dropdown__link--parent" data-nav-summary aria-expanded="false">
            <span>{{ child.title }}</span>
            {% render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-right', size: 12, class: 'dropdown__chevron' %}
          </summary>

          <div class="nav__panel nav__panel--sub" data-nav-panel>
            <div class="nav__panel-inner">
              <ul class="dropdown dropdown--sub" role="list">
                <li class="dropdown__item">
                  <a class="dropdown__link dropdown__link--all" href="{{ child.url }}">
                    {{ 'sections.header.view_all' | t: title: child.title }}
                  </a>
                </li>

                {%- for grandchild in child.links -%}
                  <li class="dropdown__item">
                    <a class="dropdown__link" href="{{ grandchild.url }}">{{ grandchild.title }}</a>
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
      {%- else -%}
        <a class="dropdown__link" href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>
